{% extends 'site/base_public.html.twig' %}

{#
   S59 PROTOTYPE, third pass.

   Pass 1 was rebuilt from nothing: 22 KB against the real page's 89 KB —
   structurally cleaner, visibly poorer, and therefore a content comparison
   rather than a layout one.

   Pass 2 started from the real markup so the card keeps the polish it already
   has in `style.css`, and grouped the grid into one section per category.

   ⚠️ Pass 2's grouping was the mistake this pass fixes. Eleven machines across
   six categories means most sections render ONE card and three empty cells,
   six times down the page. **Sections cannot fill rows** — a group of one is a
   row of one whatever you do to it. So the categories move UP into a filter
   bar, where they are *more* prominent than a heading was (always on screen,
   carrying their counts), and the grid below becomes one continuous flow with
   no holes in it. Cards stay ordered by category so the clustering survives.
#}

{% block title %}Proposition · Machines - FabOS{% endblock %}

{% block head %}<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('css/proposal.css') ~ '?v=20260801-proposal7' }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<main class="pp-wrap">
    <p class="pp-banner">
        <strong>Maquette S59 — non approuvée.</strong>
        Même contenu et même habillage que <a href="{{ path('app_machines') }}">/machines</a> ;
        seule l'organisation change.
        <a href="{{ path('app_proposition_index') }}">Index des propositions</a>
    </p>

    <div class="pp-list-head">
        <h1>Machines</h1>
        <span class="pp-headline">
            <strong>{{ freeCount }}</strong> disponible{{ freeCount > 1 ? 's' : '' }} maintenant
        </span>
    </div>

    {# ── Categories, as the primary way in ────────────────────────────────
       Not a heading per section and not a dropdown: a row of tiles that is
       always visible, carries the icon, and says how many of each kind are
       free right now — which is the number that decides whether you walk over
       there. Clicking one filters the grid. #}
    <nav class="pp-cats" aria-label="Filtrer par catégorie">
        <a class="pp-cat-tile{{ category == '' ? ' is-on' : '' }}" href="{{ path('app_proposition_machines', search ? {q: search} : {}) }}">
            <span class="pp-cat-tile-label">Toutes</span>
            <span class="pp-cat-tile-count">{{ allCount }}</span>
        </a>
        {% for tile in tiles %}
            <a class="pp-cat-tile{{ category == tile.slug ? ' is-on' : '' }}"
               href="{{ path('app_proposition_machines', search ? {cat: tile.slug, q: search} : {cat: tile.slug}) }}">
                <span class="pp-cat-tile-icon">
                    {% include 'site/proposition/_machine_icon.html.twig' with { slug: tile.slug } only %}
                </span>
                <span class="pp-cat-tile-label">{{ tile.label }}</span>
                <span class="pp-cat-tile-count">
                    {{ tile.total }}{% if tile.free > 0 %} · <span class="pp-cat-free">{{ tile.free }} libre{{ tile.free > 1 ? 's' : '' }}</span>{% endif %}
                </span>
            </a>
        {% endfor %}
    </nav>

    <form class="pp-filters pp-filters-slim" method="get" action="">
        <div class="pp-field pp-field-grow">
            <label for="pp-q">Rechercher</label>
            <input id="pp-q" type="search" name="q" value="{{ search }}" placeholder="Nom de la machine…">
        </div>
        {% if category %}<input type="hidden" name="cat" value="{{ category }}">{% endif %}
        <div class="pp-field">
            <button class="pp-btn" type="submit">Filtrer</button>
        </div>
    </form>

    {% if chips is not empty %}
        <div class="pp-chips">
            {% for chip in chips %}
                <span class="pp-chip">{{ chip.label }}<a href="{{ chip.url }}" aria-label="Retirer ce filtre">✕</a></span>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="pp-count">
        <span>
            {{ totalCount }} machine{{ totalCount > 1 ? 's' : '' }}
            {%- if totalCount != allCount %} <span class="pp-count-muted">sur {{ allCount }}</span>{% endif -%}
        </span>
    </div>

    {% if cards is empty %}
        <p class="pp-empty">
            Aucune machine ne correspond à cette recherche.
            <a href="{{ path('app_proposition_machines') }}">Voir toutes les machines</a>
        </p>
    {% endif %}

    {# ── One continuous grid. No section breaks, so no ragged rows. ──────── #}
    <div class="pp-plain-grid">
        {% for entry in cards %}
            {% set m = entry.machine %}
            {% set raw = m.statut|lower %}
            {% set down = raw in ['maintenance', 'panne'] %}
            {% set statusLabel = raw == 'maintenance' ? 'En maintenance' : (raw == 'panne' ? 'En panne' : 'Disponible') %}

            <article class="machine-card">
                <a href="{{ path('app_proposition_machine', {id: m.id}) }}" class="machine-card-link">
                    {# Favourites removed — operator decision. The status pill was
                       competing with the star and now owns the row. #}
                    <div class="machine-header pp-head-solo">
                        {# The category icon, on every card. In one continuous grid
                           there is no heading telling you what kind of thing this is,
                           so the icon does it — and it lets the eye sort the grid by
                           shape without reading a word. #}
                        <span class="pp-card-cat" title="{{ entry.catLabel }}">
                            {% include 'site/proposition/_machine_icon.html.twig' with { slug: entry.catSlug } only %}
                        </span>
                        <span class="machine-status {{ down ? raw : 'disponible' }}">{{ statusLabel }}</span>
                    </div>

                    {# The media box: a photo when there is one, the category icon
                       on a tinted tile when there is not — SAME aspect ratio either
                       way, so the grid stays even in a lab where three machines are
                       photographed and eight are not. ⚠️ `Machine.photo` is editable
                       in the admin and rendered on the public list by nothing today,
                       so this path has never run in production. #}
                    <div class="pp-media">
                        {% if m.photo %}
                            <img src="{{ m.photo starts with 'http' or m.photo starts with '/' ? m.photo : asset(m.photo) }}"
                                 alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="pp-media-icon">
                                {% include 'site/proposition/_machine_icon.html.twig' with { slug: entry.catSlug } only %}
                            </span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>

                    <div class="machine-body">
                        {#
                           ⚠️ `Machine` has NO brand and NO model column — checked. The
                           make is smuggled inside `nom`: "Imprimante 3D Ultimaker S5",
                           "Découpeuse Vinyle Silhouette". So the string that identifies
                           the machine to a member is glued to the string that says what
                           kind of thing it is, and the model cannot be searched,
                           filtered or shown on its own.

                           Until S74 splits them into real columns, the best honest move
                           is to fix the HIERARCHY with the data we have: the name is the
                           headline (it is where the model lives), the category is the
                           quiet type line under it. No parsing, no invented fields.
                        #}
                        <h3 class="machine-name pp-name">{{ m.nom }}</h3>
                        <p class="pp-type">{{ entry.catLabel }}</p>
                        <p class="machine-location">
                            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                                <path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/>
                                <circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/>
                            </svg>
                            {{ m.localisation ?? 'Localisation non renseignée' }}
                        </p>

                        {#
                           ⚠️ Two different KINDS of state, deliberately not two shades
                           of one chip. "Libre" is a fact about the machine and you
                           wait; "Formation requise" is a fact about you and you go and
                           get trained. A member who reads "indisponible" when the truth
                           is "pas formé" waits for something that will never happen.
                        #}
                        {#
                           The body now answers ONE question: is the machine itself
                           available. Whether *you* are allowed on it moved to the
                           footer — see below. That split is the availability-versus-
                           permission rule made structural instead of chromatic.

                           ⚠️ An untrained member gets the machine's state but NOT a
                           time. "Libre" is a true fact about the machine; "réservable
                           dès 08:00" would be a promise `book()` refuses, and S47's
                           rule is that we never offer a slot the checker would reject.
                        #}
                        <p class="pp-answer">
                            {% if down %}
                                <span class="pp-state pp-state-down"><span class="pp-dot"></span>Indisponible</span>
                            {% elseif not entry.authorized %}
                                <span class="pp-state pp-state-free"><span class="pp-dot"></span>Libre</span>
                            {% elseif entry.slot %}
                                <span class="pp-state pp-state-free"><span class="pp-dot"></span>Libre</span>
                                <span class="pp-next">dès <strong>{{ entry.slot.start|date('d/m à H:i', 'Europe/Paris') }}</strong></span>
                            {% else %}
                                <span class="pp-state pp-state-busy"><span class="pp-dot"></span>Complet sur 14 jours</span>
                            {% endif %}
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    {# ⚠️ The badge-tag row is gone. It carried the category and the
                       level as two chunky pills and was the tallest thing on the card
                       for the least information: the category is already the icon in
                       the header and the tile you filtered by, and both names are on
                       the detail page. Removing it is most of the vertical saving. #}
                    {# The footer is now one thing: the badge requirement. Required or
                       not — the names of the badges, and what to do about them, are a
                       click away on the detail page. The level label went with the
                       tag row; it is a qualifier, not a gate. #}
                    <div class="machine-footer pp-foot-slim">
                        {#
                           "Libre-service" rather than "Aucune formation requise":
                           it names what the member CAN do instead of the absence of
                           an obstacle, and it is the word a lab actually uses.

                           ⚠️ It stays visually quiet on purpose. Self-service is the
                           good, ordinary case; the lock is the exception, and the
                           exception is what should catch the eye. Colouring this one
                           green would also put it in competition with the green
                           "Libre" availability dot two lines above — which is exactly
                           the two-shades-of-one-chip confusion this layout removed.
                        #}
                        {% if entry.authorized %}
                            <span class="pp-req pp-req-none">Libre-service</span>
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="pp-req pp-req-yes">🔒 Formation requise</span>
                        {% endif %}
                        <span class="btn btn-sm">Voir</span>
                    </div>
                </a>
            </article>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="pp-measure">
        <strong>Coût mesuré.</strong>
        <code>{{ slotCalls }}</code> appel(s) à <code>NextFreeSlotService</code> — un par machine
        réservable — et <code>{{ elapsedMs }} ms</code> côté serveur.
        ⚠️ C'est le problème que S47 a refusé de créer : la disponibilité par carte croît
        linéairement avec le nombre de machines. À {{ allCount }} machines c'est supportable ;
        à 60 ce ne l'est plus. <strong>La vraie version a besoin de la requête groupée de S41.</strong>
        Ici <code>{{ slotCalls }}</code> seulement, parce que les machines dont la formation manque
        sont écartées avant la requête — un membre formé sur tout paierait <code>{{ allCount }}</code> appels.
    </div>
</main>
{% endblock %}
